Çevirgen

Çevirgen is a modified version of CouchSubs.
Based on CouchSubs by Sinan Yorulmaz (https://github.com/yorulmazsinan/couchsubs),
version v0.1.0-beta.88, modified from 2026-11-23 onwards.

Çevirgen is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3, like
CouchSubs. The full history of changes is in this repository's git log; the
first commit is the unmodified upstream source.

Main changes (2026-11-23):
  - New name, logo and colors; separate data folder (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Cevirgen).
  - Upstream ads, shared-pool uploads, usage statistics and the upstream update
    channel are removed or disabled; Çevirgen sends nothing to CouchSubs servers.
  - Translation is placed above the whole stacked English subtitle block.
  - Button hints split by the text recognizer are recognised and not covered.
  - Late translations stay on screen for 0.5 s instead of 2-8 s.
  - New default look (above the subtitle, no background, bold, outlined text).
  - Optional black text outline on the TV.

Changes (2026-11-24):
  - Stacked subtitles: the Turkish of an older line stays above the new line while
    its English is still on screen, and leaves with it (TV app 1.0.1).
  - User corrections ("Düzelt") that win over packs, cache and engines.
  - User glossary with "keep" / "always translate as" rules.
  - Reading speed (characters per second) per line and session summary.
  - SRT export (Turkish and bilingual) from the subtitle history.
  - Shortcut (Ctrl+H) to hide/show subtitles without stopping translation.

